    "durationMs": 168925,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener is complete and fully verified. Summary of what I built:\n\n- **API** (Spring Boot 3.4.5, Java 21): `POST /links` (auto or custom code, 201/409/422), `GET /links/{code}` (200/404), `GET /r/{code}` (302 + Location, atomic click increment), `GET /links` (ascending by id with `items`/`total`). All error responses are JSON with an `error` field; malformed JSON, bad url, and bad codes return 422.\n- **Persistence**: Spring Data JPA + PostgreSQL with a Flyway migration (`links` table with unique code constraint). Flyway applies pending migrations at startup before Tomcat accepts requests; a custom `EnvironmentPostProcessor` translates the `DATABASE_URL` PostgreSQL URL into JDBC datasource properties (no hard-coded credentials — I fixed an off-by-one in that parser found during the first startup).\n- **`sh start.sh`**: runs the prebuilt `target/app-1.0.0.jar` in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`, rebuilding with Maven only if the jar is missing.\n- **README** documents startup and the API.\n\nVerified end-to-end with curl: all status codes, exact-once click counting (1 then 3 after two more redirects), code-length boundaries (4 and 20 accepted, 3 and 21 rejected), and full data survival across a server restart. The test server is stopped, leaving port 8000 free."
  }
